  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure builds in from the west through \nmost of this week. Temps will gradually warm through the week \nas heights build. By mid to late week highs will again be back \ninto the 80s for most of the area. A backdoor front will \neventually cross the FA THU, but at this time just looks to be a\nwind shift with the column ahead of, along, and near the front \nbeing almost completely devoid of moisture.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A stronger cold front will push through the area\nFriday night, with strong high pressure building in for the weekend.\nFront looks moisture starved, but could bring sct shower \nchances. Cooler and drier airmass will build into the region \nthis weekend, feeling like fall, with highs mainly in the 60s\nand lows in the 40s/50s. N-NW winds continue to trend a bit \nstronger behind the front, which could bring dangerous marine \nconditions along with the potential for minor coastal impacts. \nThough too soon for any specifics.",
